tps://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102671#issuecomment-2649178096","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102671","id":2649178096,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6d5z_w","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-10T20:36:25Z","updated_at":"2025-02-10T20:36:25Z","body":"From a quick look though, there are more issues with the way we deal with system libraries for Wayland in `platform/linuxbsd/detect.py`. Even when `use_sowrap=no`, we still add `#thirdparty/linuxbsd_headers/wayland/` to the include path, so we take the risk of dynamically linking against a system wide version of Wayland but compiling against a different, builtin version of the headers.\n\nWe should only append the builtin headers when using sowrap.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2649178096/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]